---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AdsChecks Privacy Policy | Data Handling and Processors"
  description="Read how AdsChecks handles contact data, service inquiries, billing-related processing, and third-party processors."
  canonical="https://adschecks.com/privacy-policy/"
  ogTitle="AdsChecks Privacy Policy | Data Handling and Processors"
  bodyClass="page-privacy-policy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "AdsChecks",
      "url": "https://adschecks.com",
      "email": "contact@adschecks.com",
      "description": "Ad slot verification with proof-first reporting."
    })}></script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "item": { "@id": "https://adschecks.com/", "name": "AdsChecks" } },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "item": { "@id": "https://adschecks.com/privacy-policy/", "name": "Privacy Policy" } }
      ]
    })}></script>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-page legal-page--wide">
      <div class="doc-hero">
        <div class="doc-hero__copy">
          <p class="section__eyebrow mono">Data handling</p>
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">How AdsChecks handles contact, setup, support, and billing-related personal data.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-hero__meta">
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Controller</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v">Taras Hovorukha, Ukraine</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Primary use</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v">Setup requests, service inquiries, billing support, and website security.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Last updated</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v">24 August 2026</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-grid">
        <div class="doc-card doc-card--summary doc-card--accent">
          <h2>Controller</h2>
          <p>
            AdsChecks is operated by Taras Hovorukha in Ukraine. Responsible contact:
            <a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>Data we collect</h2>
          <p>
            We may collect your email address, company information, role, inquiry details, and other information you choose to
            submit through the website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>How we use data</h2>
          <p>
            We use your data to manage setup requests, respond to inquiries, provide commercial communication related to
            the requested service, support account or billing setup, and maintain the security and reliability of the website.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6):</strong> Processing for service delivery and billing is based on
            Art. 6(1)(b) — necessary for the performance of a contract. Processing for website security and fraud
            prevention is based on Art. 6(1)(f) — legitimate interests. Where required, we rely on consent under
            Art. 6(1)(a).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>Processors and controllers</h2>
          <p>
            Hosting and CDN are provided by <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> (processor).
            Website analytics are provided by <strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong> (processor), and only
            after you consent — see the Analytics section below.
          </p>
          <p>
            Payment processing is handled by <strong>Paddle.com Market Limited</strong> as Merchant of Record.
            Paddle acts as a separate data controller for payment-related personal data — including name, email,
            billing address, and payment method. AdsChecks does not store or process payment card details.
            Paddle's privacy policy: <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy">paddle.com/legal/privacy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            We use two categories of cookies: strictly necessary cookies, which are always active, and analytics
            cookies, which are set only if you accept them in the cookie banner. Cloudflare, which provides DNS,
            CDN, and DDoS protection for this site, may set the following strictly necessary cookies:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>__cf_bm</strong> — Cloudflare Bot Management. Set on pages protected by Cloudflare. Expires after 30&nbsp;minutes. Used to distinguish human visitors from bots.</li>
            <li><strong>_cfuvid</strong> — Cloudflare rate limiting. Set when rate-limiting rules are active. Session cookie (deleted when the browser closes). Used to apply per-user rate limits.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            These cookies are strictly necessary for the security and availability of the service. They do not track users across
            sites and do not require consent under ePrivacy rules for strictly-necessary cookies.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your cookie choice itself is stored in your browser&rsquo;s local storage under the key
            <strong>consent-analytics</strong>. This is not a cookie, is never transmitted to us, and exists only so
            that the banner does not reappear on every page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to measure aggregate website usage &mdash; which pages are
            viewed, where visitors arrive from, and approximate location at country level. We use this only to
            understand which content is useful. We do not use it for advertising, remarketing, or profiling.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Nothing is loaded until you consent.</strong> If you decline, or simply ignore the banner, the
            Google Analytics script is never requested, no analytics cookies are set, and no data about your visit
            reaches Google.
          </p>
          <p>If you accept, the following cookies are set:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>_ga</strong> &mdash; distinguishes returning visitors. Expires after 2&nbsp;years.</li>
            <li><strong>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</strong> &mdash; retains session state for the property. Expires after 2&nbsp;years.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6):</strong> consent &mdash; Art. 6(1)(a). You may withdraw consent at any
            time by clearing this site&rsquo;s cookies and local storage in your browser, which resets your choice and
            brings the banner back. Google&rsquo;s privacy policy:
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Cross-border transfers</h2>
          <p>
            Data may be processed in countries other than your country of residence, including where our service providers
            operate. We rely on appropriate safeguards provided by these processors.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain setup-request data only for as long as necessary to manage onboarding, support, and service evaluation or until you request
            deletion, unless a longer retention period is required by law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You may request access, correction, or deletion of your data and withdraw consent at any time. Contact us using the
            details above.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Data breach procedure</h2>
          <p>
            In the event of a personal data breach that is likely to result in a risk to your rights and freedoms,
            we will notify the relevant supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach,
            in accordance with GDPR Art. 33.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where a breach is likely to result in a high risk to your rights and freedoms, we will also notify
            affected individuals without undue delay in accordance with GDPR Art. 34.
          </p>
          <p>
            To report a suspected breach or security concern, contact
            <a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>Service terms references</h2>
          <p>
            Verification scope, status outcomes, pricing usage rules, and refund/dispute rules are defined on these pages:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/what-we-verify/">What we verify</a></li>
            <li><a href="/status-model/">Status model</a></li>
            <li><a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></li>
            <li><a href="/terms-and-conditions/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a></li>
            <li><a href="/refund-policy/">Refund Policy</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
